{
  "enable": "false",
  "name": "Preflight Before Script Run",
  "version": "4.0.0",
  "description": "When a variant runner or BaseExperiment script is edited, automatically run preflight validation to catch data leakage, regime violations, descending sweep errors, model-ansatz incompatibilities, and configuration issues before execution.",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "scripts/experiment_runners/run_*.py",
      "scripts/experiment_runners/verify_*.py",
      "experiments/*/exp_*.py"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A script that may define experiment variants or a BaseExperiment was just edited. The preflight tool now auto-detects the script type.\n\nRun: `.venv/bin/python scripts/preflight.py --from-script <path_to_edited_file>`\n\nThe tool will:\n- If the script has build_noiseless_variants() or VARIANTS list → run variant checks (9 validations)\n- If the script has a BaseExperiment subclass → run experiment checks (12 validations: p_layers, model_ansatz, hypothesis, h_test_unseen, h_test_valid_regime, h_values_valid_regime, descending_sweep, interpolation, n_qubits_feasibility, mpnn_capacity, seeds, restarts)\n- If neither pattern is found → report that the file doesn't match any known pattern and skip\n\nInterpret the result:\n- Exit code = 1 (ERRORS): Report the errors to the user. Do NOT execute the script until errors are resolved.\n- Exit code = 0 (clean or warnings only): Note any warnings. The script is safe to execute when requested.\n\nFor analysis scripts (analysis/run_*.py, analysis/step*.py) that don't define variants or experiments: skip preflight — it only validates variant/experiment configurations."
  }
}
